EXT. ARCTIC ICE SHELF - LIFE RAFT CAMP - DAY

A bright white world. A yellow raft hauled up on a floe, a tarp strung from poles, a single seal-oil stove. Wind sighs.

JOSEPHINE TALLCHIEF, 30s, parka hood trimmed with fur, kneels at the stove and stirs a pot. DARIUS OKAFOR, 40s, frostbitten cheeks, sits against the raft with a rifle. BERNADETTE LACROIX, 20s, in a red survival suit, stands at the edge of the floe with a radio.

BERNADETTE
(into radio)
Rescue One, this is the Meridian. Do you copy?

The radio hisses.

RESCUE ONE (V.O.)
(garbled)
...Meridian... position... say again...

BERNADETTE
We're at seventy-eight north.

RESCUE ONE (V.O.)
...hold... coming...

She grins. Turns to the others.

BERNADETTE (CONT'D)
They're coming!

JOSEPHINE
How long?

BERNADETTE
Two hours!

DARIUS
(rising)
Two hours. We can make two hours.

The floe groans. A crack zigzags across the ice between them. Josephine and Darius lunge for the raft as the floe splits, and Bernadette leaps across the gap, landing hard in Josephine's arms. All three tumble into the raft as the ice shelf shifts and a second crack opens right where the stove had been.

JOSEPHINE
Cut the line!

DARIUS ^
Cut the line!

Bernadette hacks the rope. The raft slides free. The three huddle. The stove sinks into black water.

RESCUE ONE (V.O.)
(clear now)
Meridian, we have you. Stay put.
